  "literature_notes": "L9 and L10 describe N-terminal and C-terminal HA/Flag-tagged ASIC1a constructs. ASIC1a topology places the N-terminus (residues 1\u201343) and C-terminus (residues 455\u2013528) both on the INTRACELLULAR face; these tags are therefore cytoplasmic and do not qualify as extracellular surface sites. L11 uses the same N-terminal HA construct as L9 for intracellular immunofluorescence and is excluded for the same reason. L12 describes a C-terminal mCitrine fusion, also intracellular (455\u2013528), excluded. Two extracellular sites are supported: Asp298/Leu299 (rank 1, surface_and_function) and Phe147/Lys148 (rank 2, surface_only).",
